{
  "title": "Paprika export section headers don't round-trip for digit-bearing or long labels",
  "description": "The Paprika export (server/src/api/recipes/paprika.rs, format_ingredients_text) writes a 'Section:' line before each section change. \
On re-import, detect_section_header (ramekin-core/src/ingredient_parser/item/line_classifiers.rs) only accepts generic colon-terminated labels when they're short and digit-free, unless they match another known pattern. \
So a stored section like 'Part 1' is exported as 'Part 1:' and re-imported as an ingredient line, and the following ingredients lose their section. Recognized labels are also title-cased by normalize_section_name, so the round trip isn't exact even when detection works.\n\
\n\
Paprika's ingredients field is plain text with no section syntax, so a fix probably belongs in the importer: for example, trust colon-terminated lines in a Paprika import more than in scraped HTML. Loosening detect_section_header globally risks misclassifying real ingredient lines, so check `make pipeline` diffs before doing that.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "import",
    "export",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-10-05T00:00:00-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-10-05T00:00:00-07:00",
}
